+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,4 +6,8 @@ Build through the maintained UniXNU fork with the sibling `UniXNU-Pagani_SM8750`
 
 The prior build reached the UniXNU menu and booted build 39 into the iPadOS UI. The new shared initrd driver and migrated build must be retested on hardware. Memory reservations, framebuffer stride, and embedded payload addresses remain device policy. No hardware boot is part of repository migration.
 
+`oneplus13tPkg/Applications/GpuProbe` builds the optional `OnePlus13TGpuProbe.efi` application. It uses the selected `Sm8750Platform` kit through `{tree}/kits` in `PACKAGES_PATH`; it is not dispatched as a DXE driver. The board memory map exposes one complete Device GFX aperture at `0x03D00000/0x100000`, including GPUCC, CPR and GPU SMMU. A dedicated payload menu entry runs the read-only snapshot and holds its result for a photograph until a physical key returns to the menu. See the [device test procedure](https://github.com/IssacL04/UniXNU-Pagani_SM8750#gpu-preboot-probe). GPUCC/SMMU accessibility is not yet device-verified; an external abort or a stalled bus can stop the probe at the last printed address.
+
 Original project credits and licenses remain with Mu-Silicium and the source packages. Upstream: [UniXNU/uefi-sheng](https://github.com/UniXNU/uefi-sheng).
+
+The 2026-10-30 Run 68 boot initially stopped in `CPRDxe`; adding CPR pages exposed a later `ClockDxe` access to offset `0x5080` with a zero GPUCC base. DAL/HWIO registers the entire 1 MiB GFX region, and partial GPUCC/CPR/SMMU resource HOBs conflicted with that registration. The board now supplies that complete region. The host regression and firmware/container checks pass; the user confirmed UEFI completion and XNU handoff after a temporary boot. XNU then stopped while copying SMEM for GPU board inputs. No partition was flashed.
